\f2\b 5. Copy the App Secret
\f0\b0 \
\
  Go to 
\f2\b App settings \uc0\u8594  Basic \u8594  App secret \u8594  Show
\f0\b0  and copy it. The backend rejects every webhook if this is missing.\
\
  
\f2\b 6. Set the backend environment variables (before the webhook)
\f0\b0 \
\
  Set these where the backend runs, then redeploy:\
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=<step 3>\cf2 \
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID=<step 3>\cf2 \
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=<step 4>\cf2 \
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=<step 5>\cf2 \
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=<any random string you choose>\cf2 \
  \cf3 WHATSAPP_LOG_OTP=true   # set to false once codes arrive on WhatsApp\cf2 \
\
  
\f2\b 7. Configure the webhook
\f0\b0 \
\
  1. Open the WhatsApp use case \uc0\u8594  
\f2\b Configuration \uc0\u8594  Webhook
\f0\b0 .\
  2. Enter these values:\
     - 
\f2\b Callback URL:
\f0\b0  \cf3 https://<your-backend-host>/v1/webhooks/whatsapp\cf2 \
     - 
\f2\b Verify token:
\f0\b0  the same string you used for \cf3 WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN\cf2 \
  3. Click 
\f2\b Verify and save
\f0\b0 . This only works if the backend from step 6 is already running.\
  4. Under 
\f2\b Webhook fields
\f0\b0 , subscribe to \cf3 messages\cf2 , \cf3 message_template_status_update\cf2  and \cf3 message_template_quality_update\cf2 .\
\
  
